To implement a production-grade voice agent using **Gemini Live (Native Audio)**, we will build a dedicated backend proxy to handle secure authentication and high-performance binary streaming. This architecture removes all reliance on unstable browser Speech APIs and protects your credentials by keeping them server-side.

### Phase 1: The Backend Proxy (`/voice-proxy`)

This Node.js service is designed for **Google Cloud Run**. It manages the OAuth2 handshake and pipes raw PCM audio between the client and the Vertex AI LlmBidiService.

#### 1. `voice-proxy/package.json`
```json
{
  "name": "eah-voice-proxy",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Secure WebSocket proxy for Gemini Live Native Audio",
  "main": "server.js",
  "dependencies": {
    "ws": "^8.18.0",
    "google-auth-library": "^9.15.0"
  },
  "engines": {
    "node": ">=20.0.0"
  }
}
```

#### 2. `voice-proxy/server.js`
```javascript
const WebSocket = require('ws');
const { GoogleAuth } = require('google-auth-library');

const PORT = process.env.PORT || 8080;
const LOCATION = process.env.LOCATION || 'us-central1';
const PROJECT_ID = process.env.PROJECT_ID;
const MODEL = 'gemini-2.5-flash-native-audio-preview-12-2025';

if (!PROJECT_ID) {
  console.error("ERROR: PROJECT_ID environment variable is required.");
  process.exit(1);
}

const UPSTREAM_URL = `wss://${LOCATION}-aiplatform.googleapis.com/ws/google.cloud.aiplatform.v1.LlmBidiService/BidiGenerateContent`;

const auth = new GoogleAuth({
  scopes: ['https://www.googleapis.com/auth/cloud-platform']
});

const wss = new WebSocket.Server({ port: PORT });

wss.on('connection', async (clientWs) => {
  console.log('Client connected to proxy');
  let upstreamWs = null;
  let heartbeatInterval = null;

  try {
    const client = await auth.getClient();
    const tokenResponse = await client.getAccessToken();
    const accessToken = tokenResponse.token;

    upstreamWs = new WebSocket(UPSTREAM_URL, {
      headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}` }
    });

    upstreamWs.on('open', () => {
      // MANDATORY: Send BidiGenerateContentSetup immediately
      const setupFrame = {
        setup: {
          model: `projects/${PROJECT_ID}/locations/${LOCATION}/publishers/google/models/${MODEL}`,
          generation_config: { 
            response_modalities: ["AUDIO"],
            speech_config: {
              voice_config: { prebuilt_voice_config: { voice_name: "Kore" } }
            }
          },
          system_instruction: {
            parts: [{ text: "You are Josh, a professional Elite Agent Hub receptionist. Natural tone. Short responses (<40 words). No markdown. No lists. Direct emergencies to 911." }]
          }
        }
      };
      upstreamWs.send(JSON.stringify(setupFrame));
      console.log('Gemini Session Setup Sent');
    });

    // Pipe Upstream -> Client
    upstreamWs.on('message', (data) => {
      if (clientWs.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {
        clientWs.send(data);
      }
    });

    // Pipe Client -> Upstream
    clientWs.on('message', (data) => {
      if (upstreamWs?.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {
        upstreamWs.send(data);
      }
    });

    // Keep-alive heartbeat (5s)
    heartbeatInterval = setInterval(() => {
      if (upstreamWs?.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) upstreamWs.ping();
      if (clientWs.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) clientWs.ping();
    }, 5000);

    const cleanup = () => {
      clearInterval(heartbeatInterval);
      upstreamWs?.terminate();
      clientWs.terminate();
      console.log('Session Cleaned Up');
    };

    upstreamWs.on('close', cleanup);
    clientWs.on('close', cleanup);
    upstreamWs.on('error', (err) => { console.error('Upstream Error:', err); cleanup(); });
    clientWs.on('error', (err) => { console.error('Client Error:', err); cleanup(); });

  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Failed to initialize proxy session:', err);
    clientWs.close();
  }
});

console.log(`Voice Proxy active on port ${PORT}`);
```

#### 3. `voice-proxy/Dockerfile`
```dockerfile
FROM node:20-slim
WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm install --production
COPY server.js .
EXPOSE 8080
CMD ["node", "server.js"]
```

### Phase 2: Deployment Instructions

1.  **Build & Push**:
    `gcloud builds submit --tag gcr.io/[PROJECT_ID]/voice-proxy ./voice-proxy`
2.  **Deploy to Cloud Run**:
    ```bash
    gcloud run deploy voice-proxy \
      --image gcr.io/[PROJECT_ID]/voice-proxy \
      --platform managed \
      --region us-central1 \
      --allow-unauthenticated \
      --set-env-vars PROJECT_ID=[PROJECT_ID],LOCATION=us-central1
    ```
3.  **Permissions**: Ensure the Cloud Run service account has the **Vertex AI User** role.

### Phase 3: Frontend Refactor

We update `components/VoiceAgentDemo.tsx` to use raw binary PCM streaming. The demo remains **DISABLED** via the `STREAMING_VOICE_ENABLED` flag as requested.

